<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
	Which block attributes WPML translates when a page is translated.

	WPML reads this file by itself, from the plugin root; without WPML it does
	nothing. That is why there is ONE for all modules (1.1.0; until then it
	belonged to the forms plugin): a module with attributes to translate adds
	its <gutenberg-block> entries here, in the same commit as the module. It is
	one of the three shared files (see includes/class-modules.php). What
	follows belongs to the forms module.

	How to maintain:
	- A new attribute that a person reads (visitor or recipient of an email)
	  goes in here in the same commit as in block.json.
	- Edge case: the recipient of a notification («to») is NOT translated, so
	  the translator cannot redirect the emails. If a site needs a different
	  recipient per language, it is set by hand on the translated page.
	  «name» and «formId» are not translated either: they are keys, and
	  translating them would split the submissions log and the placeholders.
	  The dropdown's «defaultOption» is not either: it is the POSITION of the
	  option, and since «options» is translated line by line without changing
	  the order, the translated page preselects the same option on its own
	  (see includes/class-preselect.php). A translator who reorders the
	  options shifts it.
	- The trap: the texts used by default when the attribute is empty (the
	  «Enviar» button, the consent) do NOT go through here, they come from the
	  .po. If they are filled in on the original site, then they do have to be
	  translated here.
-->
<wpml-config>
	<gutenberg-blocks>
		<gutenberg-block type="estrategia-web-forms/form" translate="1">
			<key name="successMessage" />
			<key name="errorMessage" />
		</gutenberg-block>
		<gutenberg-block type="estrategia-web-forms/text" translate="1">
			<key name="label" />
			<key name="placeholder" />
		</gutenberg-block>
		<gutenberg-block type="estrategia-web-forms/email" translate="1">
			<key name="label" />
			<key name="placeholder" />
		</gutenberg-block>
		<gutenberg-block type="estrategia-web-forms/tel" translate="1">
			<key name="label" />
			<key name="placeholder" />
		</gutenberg-block>
		<gutenberg-block type="estrategia-web-forms/textarea" translate="1">
			<key name="label" />
			<key name="placeholder" />
		</gutenberg-block>
		<gutenberg-block type="estrategia-web-forms/select" translate="1">
			<key name="label" />
			<key name="placeholder" />
			<key name="options" />
		</gutenberg-block>
		<gutenberg-block type="estrategia-web-forms/checkbox" translate="1">
			<key name="label" />
			<key name="privacyUrl" />
		</gutenberg-block>
		<gutenberg-block type="estrategia-web-forms/submit" translate="1">
			<key name="text" />
		</gutenberg-block>
		<gutenberg-block type="estrategia-web-forms/notification" translate="1">
			<key name="subject" />
			<key name="body" />
		</gutenberg-block>
	</gutenberg-blocks>
	<!--
		Site module (unpublished): the location, client and testimonial metas.
		The criterion (copy = the same in every language; translate = text
		that is read) and the edge case are in
		modules/site/includes/class-meta-panel.php; Meta_Panel::WPML_COPY /
		WPML_TRANSLATE say the same, and the test
		modules/site/tests/meta-panel.test.mjs fails if they do not match.
	-->
	<custom-fields>
		<custom-field action="copy">estrategia_web_location_phone</custom-field>
		<custom-field action="copy">estrategia_web_location_email</custom-field>
		<custom-field action="copy">estrategia_web_location_map_url</custom-field>
		<custom-field action="copy">estrategia_web_location_map_embed</custom-field>
		<custom-field action="copy">estrategia_web_location_static_map</custom-field>
		<custom-field action="copy">estrategia_web_location_static_map_id</custom-field>
		<custom-field action="translate">estrategia_web_location_address</custom-field>
		<custom-field action="translate">estrategia_web_location_schedule</custom-field>
		<custom-field action="copy">client_url</custom-field>
		<custom-field action="copy">estrategia_web_client_image_fit</custom-field>
		<custom-field action="translate">estrategia_web_client_business_type</custom-field>
		<custom-field action="copy">estrategia_web_testimonial_author</custom-field>
		<custom-field action="translate">testimonial_role</custom-field>
		<custom-field action="copy">estrategia_web_testimonial_rating</custom-field>
		<custom-field action="copy">testimonial_client</custom-field>
	</custom-fields>
	<!--
		Site module (1.4.3): the translation mode of the plugin's types and
		taxonomies, under their REGISTERED name (Type_Names: «eweb_» + key).
		Until 1.4.2 nothing was declared and each site set it by hand in
		WPML › Settings (Lavandería: content/semilla/cargar.mjs, WPML_MODES).

		translate="1" display-as-translated="1" is «Translatable - use
		translation if available or fallback to default language»: WPML turns
		it into mode 2 when it reads the file
		(WPML_Config_Display_As_Translated), the same mode the content-types
		module writes for its «display-as-translated»
		(modules/content-types/includes/class-wpml.php).

		THE TRAP THAT COST AN AFTERNOON (16-10-2026, WPML 5.0.2): writing
		translate="2" here, as the array of the content-types filter does,
		LOOKS like it works — the types end up in mode 2 — but WPML's XSD
		(res/xsd/wpml-config.xsd) only admits 0 or 1, and String Translation
		validates the file before reading <admin-texts>: with one invalid
		attribute the WHOLE file is dropped and no admin text of this plugin
		is registered (not even the social links), with no error anywhere.
		modules/site/tests/wpml-config.test.mjs checks the attributes. The
		filter is not affected: it never goes through the XSD.

		The criterion: ALL of them are display-as-translated. They are lists
		of items (clients, testimonials, locations, projects) shown in Query
		Loops and archives; with «translatable, only the translation» a site
		that adds a language sees every list EMPTY in it until each item is
		translated, and «not translatable» would not let anything be
		translated. Display-as-translated shows every item from day one in the
		default language, and translating it (the address and schedule of a
		location, the role in a testimonial) replaces it. The texts of each
		item are still translated or copied by the <custom-fields> above.

		Edge case, by name: a testimonial. It is a quote, usually left in the
		language it was written in; it shows as it is in /en/ and is only
		translated if someone wants to. A site where an untranslated item must
		NOT show in another language (a catalogue with prices that differ per
		country) changes that type: see the next paragraph.

		What declaring it does: WPML LOCKS the setting on its screen
		(WPML › Settings, post types; «controlled by a wpml-config.xml file»).
		A site that needs another mode for one type either ticks WPML's
		«unlock» for that type on that screen (custom_posts_unlocked_option)
		or, better because it stays in code, changes it from its theme with
		the wpml_config_array filter. And WPML applies it when it re-reads the
		files (opening WPML or Plugins in the admin, WPML_Config::load_config_run;
		Lavandería's deployer forces it), not on the next request.

		How to maintain: a new type or taxonomy of Content_Types goes in here,
		in Content_Types::WPML_MODES and in Type_Names::KEYS, in the same
		commit; modules/site/tests/wpml-config.test.mjs fails if they do not
		match. The types of each site (content-types module) do NOT go here:
		that module declares them through the filter, from each definition's
		«wpml».
	-->
	<custom-types>
		<custom-type translate="1" display-as-translated="1">eweb_client</custom-type>
		<custom-type translate="1" display-as-translated="1">eweb_testimonial</custom-type>
		<custom-type translate="1" display-as-translated="1">eweb_location</custom-type>
		<custom-type translate="1" display-as-translated="1">eweb_project</custom-type>
		<custom-type translate="1" display-as-translated="1">eweb_portfolio</custom-type>
	</custom-types>
	<taxonomies>
		<taxonomy translate="1" display-as-translated="1">eweb_client_sector</taxonomy>
		<taxonomy translate="1" display-as-translated="1">eweb_project_category</taxonomy>
		<taxonomy translate="1" display-as-translated="1">eweb_portfolio_category</taxonomy>
	</taxonomies>
	<!--
		Social module (unpublished): name and link of each network, by
		POSITION in the list («*» is the index). Reordering the list shifts the
		translations; see modules/social/includes/class-links.php. icon and
		icon_id are not translated: they are the same drawing in every
		language.

		Site module (1.4.3): the company details in «Company details»
		(estrategia_web_site) that are written in a language. WPML String
		Translation offers them in WPML › String Translation, domain
		«admin_texts_estrategia_web_site»; untranslated, every language shows
		the original. They reach the site translated through
		Company::value(), so the shortcode, the Block Bindings source and the
		WhatsApp button get them with no code of their own.

		The criterion: a detail goes in if a visitor reads it as a sentence in
		a language (an address says «Nave 14» / «Unit 14», a schedule says
		«Lunes a viernes», the WhatsApp message is a greeting, the registry is
		«Registro Mercantil de…»). Names, numbers, addresses of the internet
		and identifiers do not: Settings::WPML_SAME lists them.

		Edge case, by name: company_name. Even when it is made of words
		(«Lavandería Mallorca») it is a brand and is the same in every
		language; a site whose name really changes per language translates
		the site title (blogname), which WPML already offers.

		The trap: WPML only translates the option on the FRONT (and AJAX), not
		in wp-admin, so the «Company details» screen always shows and saves
		the original; but a REST request (/wp/v2/settings) is not wp-admin,
		and with ?lang=en it reads the translation. Content loads write
		without ?lang (measured 16-10-2026 on Lavandería local, WPML 5.0.2 +
		String Translation 5.0.2). Also: WPML registers the strings when it
		re-reads the files (see above), and only of an option that EXISTS
		then; estrategia_web_site is saved with all its keys, so the empty
		ones (a schedule not filled in yet) are registered too. And on
		Playground (SQLite) String Translation builds no .mo and translates
		nothing until its collation cache is cleared: see Lavandería's
		tests/fixtures/lm-test.php. It does not happen on MySQL.

		How to maintain: a new detail in Settings::DEFAULTS goes into
		Settings::WPML_TRANSLATE (and here) or Settings::WPML_SAME, in the same
		commit; modules/site/tests/wpml-config.test.mjs fails otherwise.
	-->
	<admin-texts>
		<key name="estrategia_web_site">
			<key name="registry" />
			<key name="whatsapp_message" />
			<key name="address" />
			<key name="schedule" />
		</key>
		<!--
			WhatsApp module (1.4.3): the button's own message option, used
			when the block's «message» is neither filled in nor bound (the
			parent theme's footer). The phone (estrategia_web_whatsapp_phone)
			is not translated. Lavandería binds the message to the company's
			whatsapp_message above instead.
		-->
		<key name="estrategia_web_whatsapp_message" />
		<key name="estrategia_web_social_links">
			<key name="*">
				<key name="name" />
				<key name="url" />
			</key>
		</key>
	</admin-texts>
</wpml-config>
